1
00:00:02,563 --> 00:00:04,314
Water.

2
00:00:04,691 --> 00:00:06,316
Earth.

3
00:00:06,859 --> 00:00:08,694
Fire.

4
00:00:09,028 --> 00:00:10,529
Air.

5
00:00:11,114 --> 00:00:15,033
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:15,368 --> 00:00:18,912
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,747 --> 00:00:22,374
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

8
00:00:22,458 --> 00:00:23,709
could stop them.

9
00:00:23,918 --> 00:00:25,460
But when the world needed him most,

10
00:00:25,586 --> 00:00:27,087
he vanished.

11
00:00:27,422 --> 00:00:31,216
100 years passed, and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

12
00:00:31,301 --> 00:00:32,968
an airbender named Aang.

13
00:00:33,177 --> 00:00:35,304
And although his airbending
skills are great,

14
00:00:35,388 --> 00:00:37,889
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

15
00:00:37,974 --> 00:00:38,974
Unh!

16
00:00:39,058 --> 00:00:42,019
But I believe Aang can save the world.

17
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:06,293
Hey, look!
A sword made out of a whale's tooth!

18
00:01:06,502 --> 00:01:07,586
Let me see that.

19
00:01:18,222 --> 00:01:19,681
This is a Water Tribe weapon.

20
00:01:19,807 --> 00:01:21,475
See if you can find anything else.

21
00:01:22,977 --> 00:01:24,269
Did someone lose something?

22
00:01:24,437 --> 00:01:25,645
No, we found something.

23
00:01:29,025 --> 00:01:30,150
It's burned.

24
00:01:31,319 --> 00:01:33,153
There was a battle.

25
00:01:33,404 --> 00:01:35,697
Water Tribe warriors ambushed
a group of firebenders.

26
00:01:36,157 --> 00:01:37,783
The firebenders fought back,

27
00:01:37,909 --> 00:01:39,409
but the warriors
drove them down this hill.

28
00:01:46,167 --> 00:01:47,626
So then what happened?

29
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:49,544
I don't know. The trail ends here.

30
00:01:49,754 --> 00:01:51,380
Wait! Look!

31
00:01:52,131 --> 00:01:53,840
It's one of our boats!

32
00:01:55,718 --> 00:01:57,260
Is this dad's boat?

33
00:01:57,470 --> 00:01:59,846
No, but it's from his fleet.

34
00:02:00,056 --> 00:02:01,098
Dad was here.

35
00:02:06,354 --> 00:02:08,063
See, Prince Zuko?

36
00:02:08,147 --> 00:02:11,733
A moment of quiet is good
for your mental well-being.

37
00:02:12,819 --> 00:02:14,694
Unh!

38
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,281
Watch out!

39
00:02:18,366 --> 00:02:19,491
Get back!

40
00:02:19,575 --> 00:02:20,742
We're after a stowaway.

41
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:22,619
There are no stowaways on my ship.

42
00:02:38,094 --> 00:02:39,678
He's paralyzed.

43
00:02:39,762 --> 00:02:41,263
Only temporarily.

44
00:02:41,514 --> 00:02:43,056
The toxins will wear off
in about an hour.

45
00:02:43,141 --> 00:02:44,433
But by then, he'll be in jail,

46
00:02:44,517 --> 00:02:45,892
and I'll have my money.

47
00:02:46,018 --> 00:02:47,686
But how did you find him on my ship?

48
00:02:48,104 --> 00:02:51,189
My shirshu can smell a rat
a continent away.

49
00:02:51,524 --> 00:02:53,108
Well, I'm impressed.

50
00:02:57,613 --> 00:02:59,990
Very impressed.

51
00:03:18,968 --> 00:03:19,968
Sokka.

52
00:03:20,052 --> 00:03:21,094
I'm coming with you.

53
00:03:21,429 --> 00:03:23,972
You're not old enough to go to war,
Sokka. You know that.

54
00:03:24,765 --> 00:03:26,433
I'm strong. I'm brave.

55
00:03:26,559 --> 00:03:27,976
I can fight!

56
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:29,436
Please, dad?

57
00:03:29,979 --> 00:03:32,481
Being a man is knowing
where you're needed the most,

58
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:36,151
and for you right now,
that's here protecting your sister.

59
00:03:36,861 --> 00:03:38,320
I don't understand.

60
00:03:38,529 --> 00:03:40,447
Someday you will.

61
00:03:41,407 --> 00:03:43,325
I'm gonna miss you so much.

62
00:03:49,499 --> 00:03:50,624
Who's there?

63
00:03:51,751 --> 00:03:52,834
Sokka?

64
00:03:52,919 --> 00:03:53,919
Bato?

65
00:03:54,086 --> 00:03:55,504
Who the what now?

66
00:03:55,713 --> 00:03:56,755
Bato!

67
00:03:56,964 --> 00:03:59,549
Sokka! Katara!

68
00:03:59,759 --> 00:04:01,760
It is so good to see you two.

69
00:04:01,844 --> 00:04:04,513
You've grown so much.

70
00:04:04,722 --> 00:04:06,014
Hi, I'm Aang.

71
00:04:06,224 --> 00:04:07,432
-Where's dad?
-Is he here?

72
00:04:07,767 --> 00:04:09,434
No. He and the other warriors

73
00:04:09,519 --> 00:04:12,270
should be in the eastern
Earth Kingdom by now.

74
00:04:15,107 --> 00:04:16,483
This is no place for a reunion.

75
00:04:16,651 --> 00:04:17,901
Let's get inside.

76
00:04:23,699 --> 00:04:24,991
After I was wounded,

77
00:04:25,076 --> 00:04:26,993
your father carried me to this abbey.

78
00:04:28,079 --> 00:04:30,747
The sisters
have cared for me ever since.

79
00:04:30,831 --> 00:04:33,250
Superior, these are Hakoda's children.

80
00:04:33,334 --> 00:04:35,210
They've been traveling
with the Avatar.

81
00:04:35,545 --> 00:04:36,836
I found them by my boat.

82
00:04:37,046 --> 00:04:39,589
Young Avatar, it gives me great joy

83
00:04:39,674 --> 00:04:40,882
to be in your presence.

84
00:04:41,217 --> 00:04:43,009
Welcome to our abbey.

85
00:04:43,386 --> 00:04:45,679
Thank you.
It's truly an honor to be here.

86
00:04:45,972 --> 00:04:47,055
If there's anything--

87
00:04:47,265 --> 00:04:48,348
What smells so good, Bato?

88
00:04:49,767 --> 00:04:52,185
The sisters craft ointments
and perfumes.

89
00:04:52,478 --> 00:04:55,230
Perfume? Maybe we could
dump some on Appa,

90
00:04:55,314 --> 00:04:56,690
because he stinks so much.

91
00:04:56,774 --> 00:04:58,191
Am I right?

92
00:05:00,528 --> 00:05:01,820
You have your father's wit.

93
00:05:03,864 --> 00:05:06,116
Bato, it looks like home!

94
00:05:06,492 --> 00:05:08,868
Everything's here, even the pelts.

95
00:05:08,953 --> 00:05:12,581
Yeah. Nothing's cozier
than dead animal skins.

96
00:05:15,084 --> 00:05:16,334
Ack!

97
00:05:18,879 --> 00:05:21,923
No way! Stewed sea prunes?

98
00:05:22,133 --> 00:05:24,009
Help yourself.

99
00:05:24,218 --> 00:05:26,177
Dad could eat
a whole barrel of these things.

100
00:05:29,473 --> 00:05:32,809
Bato, is it true you
and dad lassoed an arctic hippo?

101
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,436
It was your father's idea.

102
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,187
He just dragged me along.

103
00:05:36,272 --> 00:05:38,231
Well, the hippo did the dragging.

104
00:05:38,441 --> 00:05:40,191
Hey, I ride animals, too!

105
00:05:40,276 --> 00:05:42,193
One time, there was
this giant eel, and I--

106
00:05:42,278 --> 00:05:44,779
So, who was it that came up
with the great blubber fiasco?

107
00:05:44,864 --> 00:05:46,364
You knew about that?

108
00:05:46,574 --> 00:05:47,866
Everyone does.

109
00:05:47,950 --> 00:05:49,200
What's that story?

110
00:05:49,285 --> 00:05:50,327
It's a long one, Aang.

111
00:05:50,411 --> 00:05:51,536
Some other time.

112
00:05:51,621 --> 00:05:54,331
You and dad had
so many hilarious adventures.

113
00:05:54,707 --> 00:05:57,292
Not all of which
were hilarious at the time,

114
00:05:57,376 --> 00:05:59,794
but everything's funny with hindsight.

115
00:05:59,879 --> 00:06:00,920
Aang!

116
00:06:01,005 --> 00:06:04,299
Please put that down.
It's ceremonial and very fragile.

117
00:06:05,635 --> 00:06:08,178
Was it you or dad
that put an octopus on your head

118
00:06:08,262 --> 00:06:09,929
and convinced gran-gran
you were a water spirit?

119
00:06:10,097 --> 00:06:13,683
Your dad wore the octopus,
but I did the spooky voice.

120
00:06:16,270 --> 00:06:17,896
Aah! Unh...

121
00:06:27,531 --> 00:06:29,824
Out of my way! Step aside, filth.

122
00:06:29,909 --> 00:06:31,785
He means no offense.

123
00:06:31,994 --> 00:06:34,329
I'm certain you bathe regularly.

124
00:06:34,830 --> 00:06:36,081
I need to talk to you.

125
00:06:36,290 --> 00:06:38,333
Well, if it isn't my new friends,

126
00:06:38,542 --> 00:06:40,543
Angry Boy and Uncle Lazy.

127
00:06:40,753 --> 00:06:42,379
Heh heh heh!

128
00:06:49,303 --> 00:06:50,887
Your beast trashed my ship.

129
00:06:50,971 --> 00:06:52,263
You have to pay me back.

130
00:06:52,598 --> 00:06:53,973
Well, I'd love to help you out,

131
00:06:54,058 --> 00:06:55,475
but I'm a little short on money.

132
00:06:55,685 --> 00:06:56,976
Drinks on me!

133
00:07:02,066 --> 00:07:04,025
Money isn't what I had in mind.

134
00:07:06,153 --> 00:07:07,779
I need you to find someone.

135
00:07:07,988 --> 00:07:10,448
What happened?
Your girlfriend run off on you?

136
00:07:10,825 --> 00:07:12,200
It's not the girl I'm after.

137
00:07:12,284 --> 00:07:13,785
It's the bald monk
she's traveling with.

138
00:07:14,328 --> 00:07:15,787
Whatever you say.

139
00:07:15,871 --> 00:07:17,330
If you find them,

140
00:07:17,415 --> 00:07:19,999
I'll consider the damage
to my ship paid for.

141
00:07:20,167 --> 00:07:21,918
Ha! Forget it.

142
00:07:22,002 --> 00:07:24,754
Plus, we'll pay your weight in gold.

143
00:07:25,214 --> 00:07:27,966
Make it your weight,
and we got a deal.

144
00:07:28,342 --> 00:07:30,468
Ha ha ha! You got it!

145
00:07:30,553 --> 00:07:31,594
Get on!

146
00:07:44,316 --> 00:07:46,151
There's something
I should tell you kids.

147
00:07:46,736 --> 00:07:48,528
I'm expecting a message
from your father.

148
00:07:48,821 --> 00:07:50,780
-Really?
-When?

149
00:07:50,990 --> 00:07:52,282
Any day now.

150
00:07:52,366 --> 00:07:53,950
Your father said he'd send a message

151
00:07:54,034 --> 00:07:55,744
when they found the rendezvous point.

152
00:07:55,953 --> 00:07:58,037
If you wait here
until the message arrives,

153
00:07:58,247 --> 00:08:00,790
you can come with me
and see your father again.

154
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,418
It's been over two years
since we've seen dad.

155
00:08:03,627 --> 00:08:04,961
That would be so incredible.

156
00:08:05,045 --> 00:08:06,045
Katara!

157
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:07,672
I do really miss him.

158
00:08:08,090 --> 00:08:09,924
It would be great to see dad.

159
00:08:10,009 --> 00:08:12,427
It's been far too long,
hasn't it?

160
00:08:13,471 --> 00:08:15,054
I'm not sure when word will arrive,

161
00:08:15,139 --> 00:08:16,639
but when it does...

162
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:21,770
It would be great, but we can't.

163
00:08:21,979 --> 00:08:24,189
We have to take Aang
to the North Pole first.

164
00:08:24,398 --> 00:08:26,065
Even if we had time
to wait for the message,

165
00:08:26,150 --> 00:08:28,109
who knows how far we'd have to travel?

166
00:08:28,194 --> 00:08:30,153
We don't have time for a long detour.

167
00:08:30,362 --> 00:08:33,031
I'm sure your father would understand,

168
00:08:33,115 --> 00:08:35,784
and be proud that his children
are helping the Avatar.

169
00:08:40,247 --> 00:08:41,956
I can't believe they would leave me.

170
00:08:48,088 --> 00:08:49,756
I'm looking for Bato
of the Water Tribe.

171
00:08:49,965 --> 00:08:52,008
I know Bato.

172
00:08:52,468 --> 00:08:53,843
Make sure he gets this.

173
00:08:59,058 --> 00:09:01,226
It's the map
to Sokka and Katara's dad.

174
00:09:19,078 --> 00:09:20,578
Hey, everyone.

175
00:09:20,663 --> 00:09:21,871
Sorry I was gone so long.

176
00:09:22,122 --> 00:09:23,915
Hey, Aang. I didn't notice you left.

177
00:09:24,208 --> 00:09:26,000
Yep. But now I'm back.

178
00:09:26,210 --> 00:09:29,546
Sure could go for some
delicious sea prunes.

179
00:09:29,630 --> 00:09:31,631
Yum yum!

180
00:09:44,520 --> 00:09:46,980
Out for a bit of fresh air, are we?

181
00:09:47,147 --> 00:09:48,314
We're looking for someone.

182
00:09:48,566 --> 00:09:50,692
I hope it's not Miyuki.

183
00:09:51,110 --> 00:09:55,321
Miyuki, did you get in trouble
with the Fire Nation again?

184
00:09:56,991 --> 00:09:58,074
The Avatar's been through here.

185
00:09:58,158 --> 00:09:59,450
Let's keep moving.

186
00:10:12,131 --> 00:10:13,798
Aha! I caught you.

187
00:10:13,883 --> 00:10:16,092
You should be ashamed of yourself.

188
00:10:16,176 --> 00:10:19,095
Littering in the courtyard.

189
00:10:19,722 --> 00:10:21,389
I'm sorry. I'll take care of this.

190
00:10:27,521 --> 00:10:29,439
This ship is sentimental to me.

191
00:10:29,815 --> 00:10:31,190
It was built by my father.

192
00:10:38,449 --> 00:10:40,199
Is this the boat
he took you ice dodging in?

193
00:10:40,367 --> 00:10:42,410
Yep, and it's got
the scar to prove it.

194
00:10:42,786 --> 00:10:44,454
Ha! How about you, Sokka?

195
00:10:44,830 --> 00:10:47,749
You must have some good stories
from your first time ice dodging.

196
00:10:48,167 --> 00:10:49,584
He never got to go.

197
00:10:49,668 --> 00:10:51,169
Dad left before he was old enough.

198
00:10:51,629 --> 00:10:53,755
I forgot. You were too young.

199
00:10:54,214 --> 00:10:55,590
What's ice dodging?

200
00:10:55,674 --> 00:10:58,259
It's a rite of passage
for young Water Tribe members.

201
00:10:58,677 --> 00:11:01,054
When you turn 14, your dad takes you--

202
00:11:01,764 --> 00:11:02,805
You know what?

203
00:11:03,015 --> 00:11:04,390
You're about to find out.

204
00:11:15,277 --> 00:11:16,903
Why are we stopping?

205
00:11:17,237 --> 00:11:19,447
Because the girl must have
spent a lot of time here.

206
00:11:19,698 --> 00:11:21,074
We have no time for this.

207
00:11:24,703 --> 00:11:25,787
Hey, watch it!

208
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:28,414
- Heh heh heh!
- Look. He likes you.

209
00:11:28,666 --> 00:11:31,167
Care to hear your fortune, handsome?

210
00:11:31,335 --> 00:11:34,921
At my age, there's really
only one big surprise left,

211
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:38,466
and I'd just as soon
leave it a mystery.

212
00:11:43,931 --> 00:11:46,140
Ice dodging is a ceremonial test

213
00:11:46,225 --> 00:11:48,810
of wisdom, bravery, and trust.

214
00:11:49,144 --> 00:11:50,770
In our village,
it was done by weaving a boat

215
00:11:50,854 --> 00:11:52,605
through a field of icebergs.

216
00:11:52,898 --> 00:11:55,400
How are we supposed
to ice dodge without ice?

217
00:11:55,734 --> 00:11:58,027
You'll be dodging... Those.

218
00:12:02,366 --> 00:12:04,575
Sokka, you steer and call the shots.

219
00:12:04,952 --> 00:12:06,285
Lead wisely.

220
00:12:06,370 --> 00:12:08,329
Katara, you secure the mainsail.

221
00:12:08,622 --> 00:12:11,624
The winds can be brutal. So be brave.

222
00:12:12,126 --> 00:12:13,710
Aang, you control the jib.

223
00:12:13,794 --> 00:12:16,379
Without your steady hand,
we all go down.

224
00:12:16,797 --> 00:12:19,382
Your position is about trust.

225
00:12:19,925 --> 00:12:21,968
I know that! Why wouldn't I know that?

226
00:12:22,052 --> 00:12:25,013
I'm the Avatar! I know about trust.

227
00:12:25,889 --> 00:12:28,141
For this to be done right,
I cannot help.

228
00:12:28,475 --> 00:12:30,143
You pass or fail on your own.

229
00:12:36,692 --> 00:12:38,234
Aang, ease up on the jib.

230
00:12:38,444 --> 00:12:39,819
Katara, steady.

231
00:12:43,615 --> 00:12:44,782
Aang, less sail.

232
00:12:44,867 --> 00:12:46,659
Unh! Katara, give him room.

233
00:12:49,163 --> 00:12:50,455
Unh!

234
00:12:54,585 --> 00:12:57,545
Aang, helm to lee. Helm to lee!

235
00:12:57,629 --> 00:12:59,380
What does that even mean?

236
00:13:08,974 --> 00:13:10,558
Great job!

237
00:13:13,645 --> 00:13:14,979
There's no way through!

238
00:13:15,189 --> 00:13:16,397
We can make it!

239
00:13:16,565 --> 00:13:19,150
Sokka, you've already proven yourself.
Maybe we should--

240
00:13:19,234 --> 00:13:21,110
Aang! I'm gonna need air in that sail!

241
00:13:21,487 --> 00:13:23,696
Katara, I want you to bend
as much water as you can

242
00:13:23,781 --> 00:13:25,823
between us and those rocks.

243
00:13:26,617 --> 00:13:27,617
Now!

244
00:13:47,429 --> 00:13:50,306
The spirits of water bear witness
to these marks.

245
00:13:50,724 --> 00:13:53,851
For Sokka, the mark of the wise--

246
00:13:54,186 --> 00:13:56,687
The same mark your father earned.

247
00:13:57,147 --> 00:13:59,273
For Katara, the mark of the brave.

248
00:13:59,358 --> 00:14:01,651
Your courage inspires us.

249
00:14:02,111 --> 00:14:05,571
And for Aang, the mark of the trusted.

250
00:14:06,115 --> 00:14:09,200
You are now an honorary member
of the Water Tribe.

251
00:14:09,368 --> 00:14:10,409
I can't.

252
00:14:10,744 --> 00:14:11,828
Of course you can.

253
00:14:12,830 --> 00:14:14,872
No. You can't trust me.

254
00:14:15,082 --> 00:14:16,749
Aang, what are you talking about?

255
00:14:18,168 --> 00:14:20,128
A messenger gave this to me for Bato.

256
00:14:21,964 --> 00:14:24,590
You have to understand.
I was afraid you wouldn't--

257
00:14:24,675 --> 00:14:26,342
This is the map to our father!

258
00:14:26,426 --> 00:14:28,052
You had it the whole time?

259
00:14:28,345 --> 00:14:29,387
How could you?

260
00:14:29,638 --> 00:14:31,806
Well, you can go to
the North Pole on your own.

261
00:14:32,015 --> 00:14:33,474
I'm going to find dad.

262
00:14:33,600 --> 00:14:35,309
Now, Sokka, I think you should--

263
00:14:35,394 --> 00:14:36,644
Katara, are you with me?

264
00:14:41,233 --> 00:14:42,608
I'm with you, Sokka.

265
00:15:02,963 --> 00:15:03,963
Good luck.

266
00:15:04,339 --> 00:15:06,174
Okay. You too.

267
00:15:12,764 --> 00:15:14,223
Guess I should be moving on.

268
00:15:14,433 --> 00:15:15,808
That would be best.

269
00:15:22,399 --> 00:15:24,233
I'm an idiot, Momo.

270
00:15:44,463 --> 00:15:45,546
We're getting close.

271
00:15:55,557 --> 00:15:57,475
That wolf sounds so sad.

272
00:15:57,684 --> 00:15:59,352
It's probably wounded.

273
00:15:59,561 --> 00:16:02,355
No. It's been separated from the pack.

274
00:16:02,564 --> 00:16:04,523
I understand that pain.

275
00:16:04,733 --> 00:16:06,567
It's how I felt when
the Water Tribe warriors

276
00:16:06,652 --> 00:16:08,736
had to leave me behind.

277
00:16:08,946 --> 00:16:10,696
They were my family,

278
00:16:10,781 --> 00:16:13,366
and being apart from them
was more painful than my wounds.

279
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:23,542
Sokka?

280
00:16:23,752 --> 00:16:24,961
We need to go back.

281
00:16:25,170 --> 00:16:26,879
I want to see dad,

282
00:16:27,089 --> 00:16:28,839
but helping Aang is where
we're needed the most.

283
00:16:29,007 --> 00:16:30,007
You're right.

284
00:16:30,425 --> 00:16:32,468
Your father will understand,

285
00:16:32,678 --> 00:16:34,303
and I know he's proud of you.

286
00:16:34,513 --> 00:16:35,721
Thanks, Bato.

287
00:16:35,931 --> 00:16:37,390
I know where to go from here.

288
00:16:37,474 --> 00:16:39,600
Take this in case you want to find us.

289
00:16:39,810 --> 00:16:41,602
I'll leave a message
at the rendezvous point.

290
00:16:44,231 --> 00:16:46,107
Looks like we're going alone, guys.

291
00:16:46,191 --> 00:16:48,276
Avatar! You must leave.

292
00:16:48,527 --> 00:16:50,903
Okay, I get it.
Everybody wants me gone.

293
00:16:51,446 --> 00:16:53,572
A group of people came to the abbey
looking for you.

294
00:16:53,657 --> 00:16:54,699
Who?

295
00:16:54,908 --> 00:16:56,909
A fierce-looking woman
with a horrible monster,

296
00:16:56,994 --> 00:16:58,661
and a young man with a scar.

297
00:16:58,870 --> 00:16:59,870
Zuko.

298
00:17:00,038 --> 00:17:02,665
The beast was using the scent
of a necklace to follow you.

299
00:17:02,874 --> 00:17:04,208
A necklace?

300
00:17:04,418 --> 00:17:05,918
Katara!

301
00:17:19,433 --> 00:17:21,350
So this is your girlfriend.

302
00:17:21,435 --> 00:17:22,852
No wonder she left.

303
00:17:22,936 --> 00:17:24,270
She's way too pretty for you.

304
00:17:24,354 --> 00:17:26,439
Where is he? Where's the Avatar?

305
00:17:26,773 --> 00:17:28,482
We split up. He's long gone.

306
00:17:28,859 --> 00:17:31,068
How stupid do you think I am?

307
00:17:31,403 --> 00:17:33,279
Pretty stupid. Run!

308
00:17:35,073 --> 00:17:37,074
Aah! Unh!

309
00:17:37,451 --> 00:17:38,701
What are we supposed to do now?

310
00:17:40,829 --> 00:17:42,455
It's seeking a different scent,

311
00:17:42,706 --> 00:17:44,707
perhaps something
that the Avatar held.

312
00:17:59,723 --> 00:18:01,098
What's it doing?

313
00:18:01,183 --> 00:18:02,266
It's just going in a circle.

314
00:18:16,615 --> 00:18:17,656
-Aang!
-Up!

315
00:18:37,344 --> 00:18:38,344
Hah!

316
00:18:40,806 --> 00:18:41,972
Aargh!

317
00:18:47,562 --> 00:18:48,646
-Aah!
-Unh!

318
00:18:51,316 --> 00:18:52,358
Oof!

319
00:18:52,859 --> 00:18:53,984
Unh!

320
00:19:02,077 --> 00:19:03,160
Come on, get up!

321
00:19:32,065 --> 00:19:33,566
Unh!

322
00:19:39,906 --> 00:19:40,906
Aah!

323
00:20:00,010 --> 00:20:02,845
I'm starting to get some feeling back.

324
00:20:27,704 --> 00:20:29,121
You've got something I want.

325
00:20:50,602 --> 00:20:51,644
Aah!

326
00:20:51,853 --> 00:20:52,853
Unh!

327
00:20:59,361 --> 00:21:00,611
Oof!

328
00:21:27,222 --> 00:21:28,556
That thing sees with its nose.

329
00:21:28,682 --> 00:21:30,099
Let's give him something to look at.

330
00:21:30,183 --> 00:21:31,392
The perfume?

331
00:22:03,049 --> 00:22:06,093
June, no!

332
00:22:15,562 --> 00:22:16,937
Uncle?

333
00:22:17,022 --> 00:22:18,772
I didn't see you get hit
with the tongue.

334
00:22:19,399 --> 00:22:20,941
Shh...

335
00:22:25,238 --> 00:22:27,531
So... Where do we go?

336
00:22:27,741 --> 00:22:29,658
We're getting you to the North Pole.

337
00:22:29,743 --> 00:22:32,161
Yeah. We've lost
too much time as it is.

338
00:22:32,704 --> 00:22:33,912
Don't you want to see your father?

339
00:22:34,122 --> 00:22:35,664
Of course we do, Aang,

340
00:22:35,749 --> 00:22:37,583
but you're our family, too,

341
00:22:37,667 --> 00:22:39,126
and right now, you need us more.

342
00:22:39,461 --> 00:22:40,836
And we need you.

343
00:22:41,796 --> 00:22:43,964
I wish I could give you
a little piece of home, Katara,

344
00:22:44,174 --> 00:22:45,716
something to remind you--

345
00:22:45,925 --> 00:22:48,761
-I'll be okay.
-Still, just a little trinket.

346
00:22:48,970 --> 00:22:51,555
Maybe something like... This?

347
00:22:53,600 --> 00:22:55,517
Aang! How'd you get that?

348
00:22:55,935 --> 00:22:58,312
Zuko asked me
to be sure I got it to you.

349
00:22:59,356 --> 00:23:01,774
That's so sweet of Zuko.

350
00:23:01,983 --> 00:23:03,651
Would you give him a kiss for me
when you see him?

351
00:23:03,860 --> 00:23:04,902
Sure.

352
00:23:04,986 --> 00:23:06,820
Mwah.
